# NetHack Module — notices

The NetHack Module is distributed under the NetHack General Public License
([LICENSE.NETHACK](LICENSE.NETHACK)), independent of VectHack's own MIT
license. These notices cover what the Module carries besides the NGPL code.

## NetHack and VectHack's adaptation

NetHack (external/NetHack, and the wasm build under public/modules/nethack/)
is the official NetHack source, used under the NetHack General Public
License (NGPL). See external/NetHack/dat/license. This repository's bridge
and renderer talk to it through the windowport interface. The NetHack engine
and the NetHack-derived components -- the wasm/JS artifacts and the worker
bundle carrying src/modules/nethack/recoverSave.ts -- are NGPL-covered; the
shared renderer and the other Modules are not. See LICENSING.md.

## NetHack — non-NGPL sources

`src/isaac64.c` (the ISAAC64 RNG, written by Timothy B. Terriberry 1999-2009,
based on Robert J. Jenkins Jr.'s public-domain ISAAC) is **CC0 / public
domain**, not NGPL, and is compiled into `nethack.wasm`. It is the one file
in `external/NetHack/src/` that carries no NetHack copyright notice.

## Lua 5.4.8

NetHack 5.0 embeds Lua, so Lua is compiled into
`public/modules/nethack/nethack.wasm`. It is not part of this repository:
`scripts/build/build-nethack-wasm.sh` downloads it (sha256-verified) from
<https://www.lua.org/> at build time. Verbatim notice from `src/lua.h`:

```
